    description: "Found by the 2026-10-20 docstring-staleness audit (verifier confirmed by reading every caveat builder). verify_claims.py ~L6424-6438 builds the CAVEAT_SINK_BEFORE_SOURCE_ONLY dict with kind/flow_count/detail and no `entries`; all 16 other caveat builders set `entries`. The contract is stated in the module docstring (~L87-88), the schema-version comment (\"AT LEAST kind / entries / detail\", ~L343-345) and the ClaimVerdict.caveats field doc (~L1555). In-repo `_merge_caveat` tolerates it (`cav.get(\"entries\") or []`), so the break is external: a JSON consumer indexing caveat[\"entries\"] raises KeyError. Fix: add `entries` (the blocked flows) to that caveat."  # 1b5c
